 "title": "Proteasome Complex and ER Stress Pathway",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the proteasome complex and its role in protein degradation, particularly in the context of endoplasmic reticulum (ER) stress. The proteasome contains various subunits, including Rpt1, Rpt2, and Rpt3, and is involved in degrading substrates such as APE3 and SEC12. ER stress, induced by tunicamycin, leads to the degradation of these substrates. Additionally, site-specific photocrosslinking, conceptualized by Martin Andreas and Restrepo Santiago Yori, is used to study the ubiquitination of substrates and their interaction with the proteasome.",
